        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
          The needs.decrypt declaration and the recipient binding that open a sealed slice.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/docs/architecture/chain-of-trust/" class="group rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6 transition-colors hover:border-[var(--tb-c-accent)]" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
        <p class="tb-eyebrow">NEXT · TRUST</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-[var(--font-display)] text-lg font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)] group-hover:text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">The chain of trust</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
          Spec 09's signing chain — the authenticity decision point above every envelope.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/docs/architecture/image-formats/" class="group rounded-2xl border border-[var(--tb-c-divider)] p-6 transition-colors hover:border-[var(--tb-c-accent)]" style="background: var(--tb-c-bg-soft);">
        <p class="tb-eyebrow">NEXT · FORMATS</p>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-[var(--font-display)] text-lg font-medium text-[var(--tb-c-text-1)] group-hover:text-[var(--tb-c-accent)]">Image formats</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--tb-c-text-2)]">
          Where format-native crypto lives, and why it stays evidence.
